VDR Plugin 'vdrsternelec' Revision History
-------------------------------------------

2026-10-22: Version 0.6.0

- New menu "System functions" (main menu and setup page) and SVDRP command
  SYSTEM to run functions of VDR*ELEC's install.sh: boot program VDR/Kodi
  (-b), web components (-w), triggerhappy (-T), sample configuration (-i)
  and adding missing sample files to the configuration (-C, with a backup
  before and additional confirmations). install.sh runs in its own systemd
  unit; its output can be shown in the menu.
- VDR does not shut down automatically while a backup or a system function
  is running.

2026-10-22: Version 0.5.0

- All functions are available from the setup page (update menu, release
  servers, backups), so the main menu entry can be hidden. The setup page is
  grouped into sections.
- Backups: a backup of the VDR configuration (or of /storage/.config) is made
  before rebooting into an update (option), or on request in the OSD or via
  SVDRP BACKUP. Backups can be restored and deleted in the new menu
  "Backups & rollback"; the restore stops and restarts VDR.
- Rollback: the installed update images are kept (hard links, option "Older
  versions for rollback") and can be installed again from the backup menu.
- After the reboot, the plugin detects whether the update was installed and
  shows the result ("Last update" in the menu and in SVDRP STAT).
- Version jumps: releases of another major version are hidden and refused
  unless "Allow change of major version" is enabled.
- New option to limit the download rate while recording.
- New time window for the automatic download and the automatic reboot.
- Installed VDR*ELEC addons (e.g. cefbrowser, channellogos, yt-dlp, driver
  addons) are updated together with the system (option). Archives are checked
  before installing.

2026-10-22: Version 0.4.0

- The automatic check for updates is opt-in now (new setup option "Check for
  updates automatically", default off). Before, the plugin contacted the
  configured servers (by default the GitHub API) every 24 hours without any
  user action. Without the option, servers are only accessed when the user
  checks for updates or installs one. The check interval, notifications and
  automatic downloads are only shown and used if the option is enabled.

2026-10-21: Version 0.3.1

- Fixed: the build date of releases from a releases.json was shown two hours
  late (in CEST). Time stamps without time zone are local time now, as
  written by the LibreELEC release scripts; time stamps with time zone
  (e.g. from GitHub) are still converted correctly.

2026-10-21: Version 0.3.0

- New source type "smb": Samba shares, accessed directly with libsmbclient
  (no mount needed). Credentials in the address:
  smb://[[domain;]user[:password]@]server/share/path. Passwords are not
  shown via SVDRP and are only sent to the server of that entry.
  SMB support is built if libsmbclient is available (SMB=0 disables it).
- Local directories and SMB shares use a releases.json if there is one in
  the directory (or if the path points to a .json file). The update files
  are always taken relative to the JSON file.
- Show the build date of the installed system and of the update (OSD,
  release info, SVDRP STAT). The build date of a downloaded update is kept
  across restarts.
- Read DISTRO_ARCH/PROJECT/DEVICE/BUILD from os-release (LibreELEC >= 12).
- Copy files from local directories without libcurl.

2026-10-21: Version 0.2.0

- New source type "dir": a local or mounted network directory containing
  update files (.tar, .img.gz) and checksums (<file>.sha256 or SHA256SUMS).
  This is the "manual update" known from LibreELEC, with checksum
  verification and selection in the OSD.
- SHA256SUMS checksum lists are also supported for HTTP directory listings.
- A checksum list must contain an entry for the update file.

2026-10-21: Version 0.1.0

- Initial revision.
- Release sources: LibreELEC style releases.json, GitHub releases and plain
  HTTP directory listings.
- Download into /storage/.update with SHA-256 verification.
- OSD menus, setup page and SVDRP commands.
- Automatic check, notification, download and reboot when idle.
